## PROCEDURE
## Generation of ESC-derived cardiac progenitor cells in vitro
1| Generate mouse (option A) or human (option B) progenitor cells.
(A) Generation of mouse ESC-derived cardiac progenitor cells in vitro ● TIMING 5 d (i) Grow mESCs $(\mathsf{m E S C s}^{I s l1-C r e;\ R o s a-R F P;\ a M H C-G F P})^{26}$ on $0.1\%$ (wt/vol) gelatin-coated T25 flasks in 2i medium in a $5\%$ ${\mathsf{C}}0_{2}$ incubator set at $37^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ . Grow cells under these conditions throughout the experiment. When cells reach $70\mathrm{-}80\%$ confluence, proceed to the next step to start cell differentiation. The time to reach $70\mathrm{-}80\%$ confluence is ${\sim}3\mathrm{~d~}$ . (ii) Rinse the cells once with $\mathsf{C a}^{2+\_}$ and $\mathsf{M g}^{2+}$ -free DPBS and then dissociate into single cells by adding $1~{\mathfrak{m}}!$ of TrypLE and incubating at $37^{\circ}\complement$ for 3 min. (iii) Inactivate the TrypLE by adding $4~\mathsf{m l}$ of MEF medium. Prepare the cells for counting by diluting the resuspended cells at a 1:10 ratio in MEF medium and mixing well with a pipette. Count the cells. We use the Scepter sensor; to use this, attach the $60\mathrm{-}\upmu\mathrm{m}$ Scepter sensor to the Scepter 2.0 handheld automated cell counter and then aspirate the cells. The total cell number equals the number provided by the automated counter multiplied by ten times the total number of milliliters.  CRITICAL STEP $10\times10^{6}$ cells are needed for cell differentiation. Use the remaining mESCs for cell maintenance.   
(iv) Centrifuge $10\times10^{6}$ cells for 3 min at $270g$ at room temperature. Then aspirate the supernatant and resuspend the cells in $100~\mathsf{m l}$ of SFD. (v) Split the resuspended cells into four $150\times25\mathrm{-mm}$ sterile plates and incubate in the $5\%$ ${\mathsf{C}}0_{2}$ incubator for $48\mathrm{~h~}$ . The mESCs should form embryoid bodies (EBs) during this $48-h$ incubation. (vi) Collect all the EBs in two $50-\mathsf{m l}$ tubes and centrifuge for 3 min at $145g$ at room temperature.  CRITICAL STEP Using a low speed (145g) enables isolation of almost exclusively EBs and avoids the precipitation of single cells.   
