 CRITICAL STEP To remove the nondissociated pieces of heart tissue, filter the mix using a $100\mathrm{-}\upmu\mathrm{m}$ cell strainer.
16| Remove the supernatant and add $10~\mathrm{ml}$ of Tyrode’s solution buffer with $1\%$ (wt/vol) BSA (in PBS) and $250\upmu\mathsf{M}\mathsf{C a C l}_{2}$ and gently invert to resuspend the CM pellet.
17| Add $10~\mathrm{ml}$ of Tyrode’s solution with $0.5\%$ (wt/vol) BSA (in PBS) to the pellet in the $50\mathrm{-}\mathsf{m l}$ tube from Step 15. Invert gently to resuspend the CMs.
