Analysis of transplanted cardiomyocytes from injected rat heart $\bullet$ TIMING 1.5–5 h per heart
19| Transplanted cardiomyocytes can be analyzed in various ways. To assess sarcomere shortening and calcium transients, follow option A. To fix cells for T-tubule or other analysis, follow option B. For cDNA generation for single-cell gene expression analysis, follow option C.
## (A) Sarcomere shortening and calcium transients
(i) Aspirate the supernatant and add $10~\mathsf{m l}$ of Tyrode’s solution with $250\upmu\mathsf{M}\mathsf{C a C l}_{2}$ and invert gently to resuspend the CM pellet. Leave the tube upright for $10\mathrm{\min}$ at room temperature to let the CMs sink to the bottom. Remove the supernatant and add $10~\mathrm{ml}$ of Tyrode’s solution with $500\upmu\mathsf{M}\mathsf{C a C l}_{2}$ .   
(ii) Repeat the previous step, but add $10~\mathsf{m l}$ of Tyrode’s solution with $1\mathsf{m M}\mathsf{C a C l}_{2}$ .   
(iii) Aspirate the supernatant and add $15~\mathsf{m l}$ of Tyrode’s solution with $1\mathsf{m M}\mathsf{C a C l}_{2}$ containing $1\upmu\mathsf{M}$ of the ratiometric $\mathsf{C a}^{2+}$ indicator dye Fura-2AM and incubate for $10\mathrm{\min}$ at room temperature.   
(iv) Transfer the cells to a heated (at $37~^{\circ}\mathrm{C})$ ) perfusion chamber placed on the stage of an inverted microscope. Perfuse the CMs with Tyrode’s solution with $1\mathsf{m M}\mathsf{C a C l}_{2}$ at a flow-through rate of $2~\mathsf{m l}$ per min. Stimulate the cells at $0.5~{\mathsf{H}}z$ with electrical pulses from two electrodes placed in the perfusion chamber.   
(v) Record CM shortening by video-edge detection using the IonOptix software. Use the same software for data analysis.   
(vi) Record intracellular Fluo-3 fluorescence for $\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ transients and analyze the recorded data using pClamp v10 software27,28.
## (B) Cell fixation for T-tubule staining and analysis
(i) Plate isolated CMs in Tyrode’s solution with $\mathsf{1}\mathsf{m}\mathsf{M}\mathsf{C a C l}_{2}$ on a laminin-coated $60\mathrm{-}\mathsf{m m}$ dish and incubate in a $5\%$ ${\mathsf{C}}0_{2}$ incubator at $37^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ for $30~\mathrm{min}$ to let them attach to the dish.   
(ii) Aspirate the Tyrode’s solution and add $3~{\mathfrak{m l}}$ of $4\%$ (wt/vol) paraformaldehyde in PBS and incubate for 20 min at room temperature for cell fixation. Wash away the paraformaldehyde twice with PBS. The cells can now be used for immunostaining and nucleation assessment with DAPI staining.  CRITICAL STEP For confocal microscopy analysis, plate the cells on laminin-coated coverslips.  PAUSE POINT The cells can be stained immediately or after overnight storage at $4^{\circ}\complement$ .   
(iii) Block the fixed cells with $1\%$ (wt/vol) BSA in PBS by incubating for $1\mathfrak{h}$ at room temperature. For T-tubule staining, add Fluor-594-conjugated WGA antibody at a 1:1,000 dilution and incubate at $4^{\circ}\complement$ overnight. Wash the cells twice for 5 min with PBS.  CRITICAL STEP Avoid shorter incubation times to prevent low intensity of the staining. $\blacktriangle$ CRITICAL STEP Alternative antibody combinations can be substituted, and standard immunofluorescence staining performed.   
(iv) Add DAPI to stain the nuclei, and incubate for 10 min at room temperature. (v) Wash the cells twice for 5 min with PBS and mount the cells with ProLong Diamond antifade mount.  PAUSE POINT The cells can either be imaged immediately or stored overnight at $4^{\circ}\complement$ and imaged the next day.   
(vi) Image the T-tubules using a confocal microscope with a 403 (1.15 numerical aperture) oil-immersion lens.   
(vii) Analyze WGA staining using ImageJ. Apply a median filter, create a binary mask of the WGA signal using the Auto Local Threshold plugin and erode the mask once.   
(viii) Create a region of interest in each cell. Exclude the boundary membrane to isolate the T-tubule network for segmentation analysis.   
(ix) Use the Analyze Particles plugin to measure the T-tubule area $(\mathsf{m m}^{2})$ , which is normalized to the total cell area to calculate the fractional area. $\blacktriangle$ CRITICAL STEP Compare two groups using a two-tailed t test. Use the same optical field for statistical comparison between host CMs and in vivo-matured CMs to eliminate staining errors.
## (C) cDNA generation for single-cell gene expression analysis
(i) Use a $20\mathrm{-}\upmu\updownarrow$ pipette to manually pick the isolated $6F P+/R F P+$ CMs (in Tyrode’s solution) under a fluorescence microscope (EVOS). Transfer each cell to a single well of a 96-well plate containing $2.4~\upmu\upiota$ of RNase-free water, $0.2~\upmu\upiota$ of RNase-free DNase I and $0.25~\upmu\upiota$ of RNase inhibitor.   
(ii) Incubate at $72^{\circ}\mathfrak{C}$ for 3 min to inactivate DNase I and then quench on ice. Add $1\upmu\upiota$ of custom-designed primer (with 30-deoxythymidine anchor) and transfer to $72^{\circ}\mathfrak{C}$ for 2 min to anneal to polyadenylated RNA and then quench on ice.   
(iii) Add a mixture of $1\upmu\upiota$ of SMARTScribe reverse transcriptase, $1\upmu\upiota$ of custom-designed TSO oligo $(12{\mathsf{m M}})$ , $0.3~\upmu\upiota$ of $\mathsf{M g C l}_{2}$ $(200~\mathsf{m M})$ , $0.5~{\upmu\updownarrow}$ of RNase inhibitor, $1\upmu\upiota$ of dNTP mix and $0.25~\upmu\updownarrow$ of DTT $(100~\mathsf{m M})$ , and incubate at $42^{\circ}\complement$ for $90~\mathrm{min}$ , followed by enzyme inactivation at $70~^{\circ}\complement$ for $10\mathrm{\min}$ .   
(iv) Add a mixture of $29\upmu\upiota$ of water, $5\upmu\upiota$ of Advantage 2 taq polymerase buffer, $2~{\upmu\updownarrow}$ of dNTPs, $2~\upmu\upiota$ of custom-designed amplifying PCR primer $(12{\mathsf{m M}})$ and $2~{\upmu\updownarrow}$ of Advantage 2 taq polymerase to the reverse transcription product and
amplify for 20 cycles using the following program:
(v) Purify the amplification product using Ampure XP beads. Use the cDNA to test gene expression by $q{\mathsf{P C R}}$ or perform RNA sequencing based on previously published protocols21,29.
